    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28525" root="عر" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعَرُّ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَارٌّ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  One says also, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنْتَ شَرٌّ مِنْهُ وَأَعَرُّ</span>
[meaning (assumed tropical:)  <i>Thou art worse than he, and more
evil:</i> the two nouns being synonymous, like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرٌّ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَرٌّ</span>]. (TA.)

